real CMs\\\"\"\n55\t          ]\n56\t        ]\n57\t      }\n58\t    ],\n59\t    \"figures\": [],\n60\t    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 的核心 attack 不是 exp-001 结果本身不好，而是 synthetic-only validation  在 exp-004/015/016 negative 结果面前失去说服力。exp-001 被重新定性为  \\\"method works under favorable assumptions that don't hold in practice\\\"。 在 worst 档 reframe 下，exp-001 数据可以保留但重新定位为  \\\"controlled validation confirming implementation correctness\\\"，不再作为 method effectiveness 的 evidence。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下，reviewer 完全承认 HB 在 synthetic 上 works，但判定： (a) 4-9% RMSE improvement over MLE 是 \\\"modest, well-known partial pooling benefit\\\"， 任何 Bayesian textbook 都有的 James-Stein shrinkage 效应； (b) synthetic DGP 是 symmetric misclassification（FPR=FNR），人为有利于 CM inversion ——  real LLM misclassification 是 highly asymmetric（exp-004: FNR=53%），这使得 synthetic 结果不可外推； (c) coverage 0.87-0.93 in worst configs 低于 nominal 0.95，但 reviewer 不会 flag 这个 ——  他们的 attack vector 是 \\\"works on synthetic, fails on real\\\"，不是 synthetic 内部的 calibration； (d) hyperprior sensitivity 4-5% 在 K=4 被视为 \\\"acceptable but unremarkable\\\"。 总体判定：exp-001 是 competent engineering，不是 contribution。\\n\"\n61\t  },\n62\t  {\n63\t    \"name\": \"Bias Identity Verification\",\n64\t    \"description\": \"Formal bias decomposition verification: bias = f(Δπ, Δτ) identity\",\n65\t    \"results\": {\n66\t      \"r2_k2\": 0.9939,\n67\t      \"r2_k4\": 0.9738,\n68\t      \"tightness_ratio_k2_median\": 1.0027,\n69\t      \"tightness_ratio_k4_median\": 1.0234,\n70\t      \"debiasing_hurts_pct\": 50,\n71\t      \"max_bias_ratio_k2\": 2.86,\n72\t      \"max_bias_ratio_k4\": 2.41,\n73\t      \"reviewer_novelty_assessment\": \"textbook re-derivation\",\n74\t      \"carroll_overlap_pct\": 85\n75\t    },\n76\t    \"tables\": [\n77\t      {\n78\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: Bias Identity R² and Reviewer Assessment\",\n79\t        \"columns\": [\n80\t          \"K\",\n81\t          \"R²\",\n82\t          \"Tightness Ratio\",\n83\t          \"Reviewer Comment\"\n84\t        ],\n85\t        \"rows\": [\n86\t          [\n87\t            \"2\",\n88\t            \"0.9939\",\n89\t            \"1.0027\",\n90\t            \"\\\"Exact — but this IS the classical result\\\"\"\n91\t          ],\n92\t          [\n93\t            \"4\",\n94\t            \"0.9738\",\n95\t            \"1.0234\",\n96\t            \"\\\"Slight deviation from identity = finite-sample noise, not new insight\\\"\"\n97\t          ]\n98\t        ]\n99\t      },\n100\t      {\n101\t        \"name\": \"Table 3: Debiasing-Hurts Regions\",\n102\t        \"columns\": [\n103\t          \"Scenario\",\n104\t          \"Bias Ratio\",\n105\t          \"Δπ threshold\",\n106\t          \"Reviewer Comment\"\n107\t        ],\n108\t        \"rows\": [\n109\t          [\n110\t            \"K=2/extreme\",\n111\t            \"2.86x\",\n112\t            \"0.1235\",\n113\t            \"\\\"Known: overcorrection when correction model misspecified\\\"\"\n114\t          ],\n115\t          [\n116\t            \"K=4/extreme\",\n117\t            \"2.41x\",\n118\t            \"0.1235\",\n119\t            \"\\\"Same mechanism, different K\\\"\"\n120\t          ],\n121\t          [\n122\t            \"K=2/moderate\",\n123\t            \"1.2x\",\n124\t            \"0.1235\",\n125\t            \"\\\"Marginal effect — who cares?\\\"\"\n126\t          ]\n127\t        ]\n128\t      }\n129\t    ],\n130\t    \"figures\": [],\n131\t    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档的 kill shot #1。当 measurement error 专家在 panel 上时， Theorem 1 的 novelty claim 被直接否定。R² = 0.99 paradoxically 证明了这 IS 一个 known result  （如果是 novel，empirical verification 不该如此 clean）。 Reframe 方向：降级为 \\\"consistent with classical ME theory, we verify the product-form  identity holds empirically across LLM annotation settings\\\"，不再 claim formal novelty。 关键：reframe 后这个 experiment 仍有价值，因为 \\\"verifying classical theory holds  in the LLM annotation context\\\" 是 valid empirical contribution，但需要 proper citation。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档的 defining assumption：reviewer panel 包含 measurement error 专家，直接指出  Theorem 1 是 Carroll et al. (2006, Ch.4) 的 special case。具体论证： (a) \\\"bias ∝ Δπ × Δτ product form\\\" 是 classical ME literature 中 \\\"bias amplification  under misspecified correction model\\\" 的 well-known result，只是 notation 不同； (b) R² = 0.99 证明 identity holds，但 \\\"verifying a known identity empirically\\\" 不是 contribution； (c) \\\"debiasing hurts in 50% of parameter space\\\" 被视为 \\\"trivially follows from the identity —  whenever Δπ and Δτ have the right sign combination, overcorrection occurs, this is Definition 4.2 in Carroll\\\"； (d) max bias ratio 2.86x / 2.41x 被视为 \\\"interesting empirically but theoretically unsurprising\\\"； (e) K=2 vs K=4 non-monotonicity（2.86 vs 2.41 for DIM）被视为 \\\"artifact of the specific estimator,  not a deep structural insight\\\"。 Reviewer 会写：\\\"The authors present Theorem 1 as a novel contribution, but the product-form  relationship between misclassification heterogeneity and bias amplification is a standard result  in the measurement error literature (Carroll et al. 2006, Fuller 1987). The empirical verification  with R²>0.97 is reassuring but not surprising.\\\"\\n\"\n132\t  },\n133\t  {\n134\t    \"name\": \"Semi-Synthetic CSS Benchmark\",\n135\t    \"description\": \"Semi-synthetic benchmark using TweetEval sentiment with injected CATE structure\",\n136\t    \"results\": {\n137\t      \"n_subgroups\": 4,\n138\t      \"misclass_rates\": \"S0=0.05, S1=0.10, S2=0.15, S3=0.25\",\n139\t      \"p_z1_actual\": 0.39,\n140\t      \"debiasing_hurts_confirmed\": true,\n141\t      \"hb_vs_mle_n100_S3_extreme\": \"+60% RMSE improvement\",\n142\t      \"hb_vs_mle_n50_S3_extreme\": \"-57% RMSE (HB worse)\",\n143\t      \"boundary_condition\": \"n_expert >= 100\",\n144\t      \"reviewer_perceived_validity\": \"low — DGP designed to favor method\"\n145\t    },\n146\t    \"tables\": [\n147\t      {\n148\t        \"name\": \"Table 4: Semi-Synthetic Results vs Reviewer Perception\",\n149\t        \"columns\": [\n150\t          \"Config\",\n151\t          \"HB RMSE Δ vs MLE\",\n152\t          \"Actual Validity\",\n153\t          \"Reviewer Perception\"\n154\t        ],\n155\t        \"rows\": [\n156\t          [\n157\t            \"n=50/S3/extreme\",\n158\t            \"-57%\",\n159\t            \"Boundary condition\",\n160\t            \"\\\"Method fails at practical budgets\\\"\"\n161\t          ],\n162\t          [\n163\t            \"n=100/S3/extreme\",\n164\t            \"+60%\",\n165\t            \"Strong result\",\n166\t            \"\\\"Only works because P(Z=1)=0.39 and symmetric CM\\\"\"\n167\t          ],\n168\t          [\n169\t            \"n=250/S3\",\n170\t            \"+5-17%\",\n171\t            \"Moderate gain\",\n172\t            \"\\\"Modest, not worth the complexity\\\"\"\n173\t          ],\n174\t          [\n175\t            \"n=500/all\",\n176\t            \"+0.2-1.6%\",\n177\t            \"Converged\",\n178\t            \"\\\"At this budget, any method works\\\"\"\n179\t          ]\n180\t        ]\n181\t      }\n182\t    ],\n183\t    \"figures\": [],\n184\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-003 的 semi-synthetic 结果在 worst 档下被 reframed 为 \\\"controlled validation  that confirms implementation correctness under favorable conditions\\\"。 关键问题不是 exp-003 结果错误，而是它不能 generalize： 当 P(Z=1) 从 0.39 降到 0.18（real data），per-subgroup expert labels  急剧减少，HB estimation noise 吞没 bias correction gain。 这 exactly 是 exp-015/016 观察到的 pattern。Reviewer 将此称为 \\\"overfitting to simulation\\\"。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 reviewer 对 exp-003 的攻击角度： (a) \\\"Semi-synthetic\\\" DGP 是 author-designed：CATE heterogeneity 是 injected 的， misclassification rates 是 hand-picked 的，treatment assignment 是 controlled 的 ——  \\\"the authors designed a DGP where their method works, then showed it works\\\"； (b) misclass_rates S0=0.05 到 S3=0.25 的 spread（Δπ=0.20）被视为 \\\"optimistic —  real-world Δπ in exp-004 is only 0.117, and in exp-012 pilot is 0.098-0.200 depending on grouping\\\"； (c) P(Z=1)=0.39 被视为 \\\"unrealistically high — CivilComments P(Z=1)=0.18,  most real datasets have severe class imbalance that exp-003 avoids\\\"； (d) n=50 boundary condition 被 acknowledged 但 n=100 recommendation 被视为  \\\"will be violated in real per-subgroup settings with K=4+ and small expert budgets\\\"； (e) 整个 semi-synthetic 在 exp-015/016 negative 面前被 recharacterized 为  \\\"overfitting to favorable simulation conditions\\\"。\\n\"\n185\t  },\n186\t  {\n187\t    \"name\": \"Real-Data Case Study (Pattern Consistency)\",\n188\t    \"description\": \"Real CSS dataset (UC Berkeley Hate Speech) with subgroup-varying LLM misclassification\",\n189\t    \"results\": {\n190\t      \"dataset\": \"UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech\",\n191\t      \"n_comments\": 2496,\n192\t      \"delta_pi\": 0.117,\n193\t      \"global_FNR\": 0.533,\n194\t      \"avg_abs_bias_naive\": 0.21,\n195\t      \"avg_abs_bias_global\": 0.273,\n196\t      \"avg_abs_bias_ec_hte\": 0.313,\n197\t      \"ec_hte_worse_than_global\": true,\n198\t      \"ec_hte_worse_than_naive\": true,\n199\t      \"reviewer_verdict\": \"fatal — method fails on real data\"\n200\t    },\n201\t    \"tables\": [\n202\t      {\n203\t        \"name\": \"Table 5: Real-Data Results — The Fatal Evidence\",\n204\t        \"columns\": [\n205\t          \"Method\",\n206\t          \"Avg |Bias|\",\n207\t          \"Rank\",\n208\t          \"Reviewer Interpretation\"\n209\t        ],\n210\t        \"rows\": [\n211\t          [\n212\t            \"Naive\",\n213\t            \"0.210\",\n214\t            \"1 (best)\",\n215\t            \"\\\"Doing nothing is better than the proposed method\\\"\"\n216\t          ],\n217\t          [\n218\t            \"Global Corrected\",\n219\t            \"0.273\",\n220\t            \"2\",\n221\t            \"\\\"Simple baseline outperforms\\\"\"\n222\t          ],\n223\t          [\n224\t            \"EC-HTE (proposed)\",\n225\t            \"0.313\",\n226\t            \"3 (worst)\",\n227\t            \"\\\"Method INCREASES bias on real data\\\"\"\n228\t          ]\n229\t        ]\n230\t      },\n231\t      {\n232\t        \"name\": \"Table 6: Cross-Validation with exp-015/016\",\n233\t        \"columns\": [\n234\t          \"Experiment\",\n235\t          \"Real CMs Source\",\n236\t          \"HB vs Global RMSE\",\n237\t          \"Verdict\"\n238\t        ],\n239\t        \"rows\": [\n240\t          [\n241\t            \"exp-004\",\n242\t            \"UC Berkeley direct\",\n243\t            \"HB worse\",\n244\t            \"\\\"Fatal\\\"\"\n245\t          ],\n246\t          [\n247\t            \"exp-015\",\n248\t            \"GPT-4.1 pilot CMs\",\n249\t            \"HB 3-4x worse\",\n250\t            \"\\\"Confirmed fatal\\\"\"\n251\t          ],\n252\t          [\n253\t            \"exp-016\",\n254\t            \"GPT-3.5 CMs\",\n255\t            \"HB 3.5-5x worse\",\n256\t            \"\\\"Triply confirmed\\\"\"\n257\t          ]\n258\t        ]\n259\t      }\n260\t    ],\n261\t    \"figures\": [],\n262\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-004 的 negative result 在 worst 档下无法 mitigate，只能 reframe。 Reframe 策略：这个 negative result BECOMES the core contribution ——  \\\"we show that standard corrections fail on real data, and we characterize exactly  why (FNR > 0.4 + P(Z=1) < 0.2 → insufficient per-subgroup positive-class expert labels)\\\"。 这是 \\\"When Debiasing Hurts\\\" 的 literal embodiment。 但 reviewer 的反驳是：\\\"problem identification without solution is not sufficient  for EMNLP main — you've shown the problem exists, now what?\\\"\\n\\n\\n这是 worst 档的 kill shot #2，也是最具破坏力的 evidence。 Reviewer 论证链： (a) EC-HTE avg |bias| = 0.313 > Global 0.273 > Naive 0.21 ——  \\\"the proposed method is WORST among all options on real data\\\"； (b) 作者 frame 为 \\\"inconclusive due to wide bootstrap CIs\\\"，但 reviewer 反驳： \\\"wide CIs are themselves evidence of the method's impracticality —  if you can't get tight enough CIs to demonstrate improvement on 2496 samples,  the method doesn't scale to realistic settings\\\"； (c) global FNR = 53% 被视为 \\\"typical of real LLM annotation\\\" 而非 \\\"edge case\\\" ——  \\\"if the method breaks whenever FNR > 0.4, it's not useful for real NLP tasks  where LLMs systematically under-detect minority categories\\\"； (d) Δπ = 0.117 is \\\"moderate, not extreme\\\" —— \\\"the method needs extreme heterogeneity  to work, but real heterogeneity is moderate\\\"； (e) exp-015 (GPT-4.1 CMs) 和 exp-016 (GPT-3.5 CMs) 用 controlled semi-synthetic  确认了 same failure pattern —— \\\"this is not a dataset artifact, it's a systematic failure\\\"。 Reviewer 会写：\\\"The real-data evaluation (Section 5.3) is the most informative result  in the paper, and it is negative. EC-HTE produces higher bias than both the naive estimator  and global correction on the UC Berkeley Hate Speech corpus. The authors attribute this  to high FNR, but high FNR is the norm in real LLM annotation tasks, not the exception.  A method that only works when the classifier is already good enough is of limited practical value.\\\"\\n\"\n263\t  },\n264\t  {\n265\t    \"name\": \"Diagnostic Criterion Validation\",\n266\t    \"description\": \"Diagnostic criterion: Δπ × Δτ predicts when global correction fails\",\n267\t    \"results\": {\n268\t      \"subgroup_level_auc\": 0.833,\n269\t      \"setting_level_auc\": 0.49,\n270\t      \"low_pi_hurt_pct\": 84.6,\n271\t      \"reviewer_verdict\": \"contribution failure — AUC 0.49 at actionable level\"\n272\t    },\n273\t    \"tables\": [\n274\t      {\n275\t        \"name\": \"Table 7: Diagnostic AUC — Claim vs Evidence\",\n276\t        \"columns\": [\n277\t          \"Level\",\n278\t          \"AUC\",\n279\t          \"Actionable?\",\n280\t          \"Reviewer Verdict\"\n281\t        ],\n282\t        \"rows\": [\n283\t          [\n284\t            \"Subgroup\",\n285\t            \"0.833\",\n286\t            \"No (requires true CATE)\",\n287\t            \"\\\"Circular — needs what you're trying to estimate\\\"\"\n288\t          ],\n289\t          [\n290\t            \"Setting\",\n291\t            \"0.490\",\n292\t            \"Yes (but fails)\",\n293\t            \"\\\"Worse than coin flip\\\"\"\n294\t          ],\n295\t          [\n296\t            \"Asymmetric (exp-028)\",\n297\t            \"0.611-0.626\",\n298\t            \"No\",\n299\t            \"\\\"Marginal improvement, still useless\\\"\"\n300\t          ]\n301\t        ]\n302\t      }\n303\t    ],\n304\t    \"figures\": [],\n305\t    \"analysis\": \"Diagnostic 在 worst 档下被判定为 complete failure。 Reframe 策略：abandon AUC-based prediction entirely，转为  \\\"empirical rule of thumb: if Δπ > 0.10, check before applying global correction\\\"。 这不是 formal diagnostic，而是 practitioner guideline ——  类似 \\\"if VIF > 10, worry about multicollinearity\\\" 的 heuristic。 但 reviewer 可能仍会质疑：\\\"this threshold was derived from your own synthetic data,  how do we know it generalizes?\\\"\\n\\n\\nWorst 档的 kill shot #3。Reviewer 论证： (a) Setting-level AUC = 0.49 是 \\\"literally worse than random\\\" ——  \\\"the diagnostic cannot predict at the level where practitioners need to make decisions  (should I use global or stratified correction for THIS dataset?)\\\"； (b) Subgroup-level AUC = 0.833 被 dismissed： \\\"subgroup-level prediction is not actionable — a practitioner doesn't know true subgroup CATEs  at decision time, so they can't compute the diagnostic at subgroup level\\\"； (c) \\\"84.6% of low-Δπ settings hurt\\\" 是 \\\"a marginal distribution, not a prediction\\\" ——  \\\"knowing that low heterogeneity settings tend to be hurt by correction is trivially obvious  from the bias identity; the diagnostic adds no information beyond the identity itself\\\"； (d) exp-028 进一步确认 asymmetric diagnostic 也 fails（overall AUC 0.626, K=2 all zero）； (e) reviewer 会将 Claim 3 标记为 \\\"not supported by the evidence\\\" 并要求删除或  大幅 downgrade。 Reviewer 会写：\\\"The diagnostic criterion (Claim 3) is presented as a practical tool,  but its setting-level AUC of 0.49 means it cannot distinguish settings where global correction  helps from those where it hurts. The subgroup-level AUC of 0.833 is not actionable because  the required quantities (true subgroup CATEs) are unknown at decision time.  This contribution should be removed or reformulated as a negative result.\\\"\\n\"\n306\t  },\n307\t  {\n308\t    \"name\": \"Expert Label Budget Sensitivity\",\n309\t    \"description\": \"Systematic sweep of n_expert × K × regime for crossover point\",\n310\t    \"results\": {\n311\t      \"crossover_K2_extreme\": 250,\n312\t      \"crossover_K2_moderate\": \"never\",\n313\t      \"crossover_K4_extreme\": 1000,\n314\t      \"crossover_K4_moderate\": 2000,\n315\t      \"hb_vs_mle_wins\": \"21/24 (87.5%)\",\n316\t      \"reviewer_verdict\": \"impractical budgets in moderate regime\"\n317\t    },\n318\t    \"tables\": [\n319\t      {\n320\t        \"name\": \"Table 8: Crossover Points — Reviewer Interpretation\",\n321\t        \"columns\": [\n322\t          \"Config\",\n323\t          \"Crossover n_expert\",\n324\t          \"Practical?\",\n325\t          \"Reviewer Comment\"\n326\t        ],\n327\t        \"rows\": [\n328\t          [\n329\t            \"K=2/extreme\",\n330\t            \"250\",\n331\t            \"Marginal\",\n332\t            \"\\\"Only practical scenario, but extreme regime is rare\\\"\"\n333\t          ],\n334\t          [\n335\t            \"K=2/moderate\",\n336\t            \"Never\",\n337\t            \"No\",\n338\t            \"\\\"Method never helps in common scenario\\\"\"\n339\t          ],\n340\t          [\n341\t            \"K=4/extreme\",\n342\t            \"1000\",\n343\t            \"No\",\n344\t            \"\\\"Budget exceeds most research projects\\\"\"\n345\t          ],\n346\t          [\n347\t            \"K=4/moderate\",\n348\t            \"2000\",\n349\t            \"No\",\n350\t            \"\\\"At 2000 labels, use experts directly\\\"\"\n351\t          ]\n352\t        ]\n353\t      }\n354\t    ],\n355\t    \"figures\": [],\n356\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-006 在 worst 档下成为 \\\"method's own evidence against itself\\\"。 核心问题：EC-HTE 的 value proposition 是 \\\"use LLM labels cheaply + few expert labels for calibration\\\"， 但 crossover analysis 显示 calibration 本身需要大量 expert labels， 侵蚀了 cost-effectiveness argument。 Reframe：转为 \\\"budget guidelines for practitioners\\\" —— 不是 \\\"EC-HTE 需要多少 labels\\\"  而是 \\\"any correction method 在低 budget 时不如 naive\\\"。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 reviewer 的解读： (a) K=2/moderate \\\"never crosses\\\" = \\\"in the most common real-world scenario  (moderate heterogeneity, binary subgroups), EC-HTE NEVER outperforms global on RMSE\\\"； (b) K=4/extreme crossover at n=1000 experts = \\\"who has 1000 expert-labeled samples  for calibration? At that budget, just use expert labels directly for CATE estimation\\\"； (c) K=4/moderate crossover at n=2000 = \\\"absurd — 2000 expert labels for 4 subgroups  means 500/subgroup, at which point expert-only estimation is viable\\\"； (d) K=2/extreme crossover at n=250 是 \\\"the only practical scenario,  but extreme heterogeneity is rare in real data (exp-004 Δπ=0.117 is moderate)\\\"； (e) HB vs MLE 21/24 wins 被 dismissed as \\\"improvement over the wrong baseline —  the question is HB vs Global, not HB vs MLE\\\"。 总结：reviewer 将 exp-006 解读为 \\\"the method's own budget analysis shows  it's impractical except in rare extreme-heterogeneity scenarios\\\"。\\n\"\n357\t  },\n358\t  {\n359\t    \"name\": \"PPCI + DSL Baseline Comparison\",\n360\t    \"description\": \"PPCI/DSL baselines, EC-HTE+PPCI composition for dual-error scenarios\",\n361\t    \"results\": {\n362\t      \"dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_ppci_bias\": 0.005,\n363\t      \"dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ppci_alone_bias\": 0.004,\n364\t      \"dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_alone_bias\": 0.178,\n365\t      \"ec_hte_ppci_rmse\": 0.225,\n366\t      \"ppci_alone_rmse\": 0.261,\n367\t      \"reviewer_verdict\": \"PPCI alone achieves same bias reduction — why add EC-HTE?\"\n368\t    },\n369\t    \"tables\": [\n370\t      {\n371\t        \"name\": \"Table 9: DGP C (Both Errors) — PPCI vs EC-HTE+PPCI\",\n372\t        \"columns\": [\n373\t          \"Method\",\n374\t          \"|Bias|\",\n375\t          \"RMSE\",\n376\t          \"Reviewer Verdict\"\n377\t        ],\n378\t        \"rows\": [\n379\t          [\n380\t            \"PPCI alone\",\n381\t            \"0.004\",\n382\t            \"0.261\",\n383\t            \"\\\"Sufficient — simpler, nearly same bias\\\"\"\n384\t          ],\n385\t          [\n386\t            \"EC-HTE+PPCI\",\n387\t            \"0.005\",\n388\t            \"0.225\",\n389\t            \"\\\"Marginal RMSE gain, not worth complexity\\\"\"\n390\t          ],\n391\t          [\n392\t            \"EC-HTE alone\",\n393\t            \"0.178\",\n394\t            \"0.226\",\n395\t            \"\\\"Cannot handle outcome error\\\"\"\n396\t          ],\n397\t          [\n398\t            \"Naive\",\n399\t            \"0.251\",\n400\t            \"0.269\",\n401\t            \"\\\"EC-HTE alone barely beats naive\\\"\"\n402\t          ]\n403\t        ]\n404\t      }\n405\t    ],\n406\t    \"figures\": [],\n407\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-007 在 worst 档下暴露了 EC-HTE 的 marginal value： 当 PPCI 已经 available 时，EC-HTE 的 additional contribution 仅是 14% RMSE reduction。 Reviewer 将此定性为 \\\"incremental improvement over existing method,  not a new paradigm\\\"。 Reframe：在 \\\"When Debiasing Hurts\\\" 版本中，PPCI comparison  成为 \\\"what practitioners should use instead\\\" 的 recommendation。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 reviewer 的 devastating observation： (a) DGP C（both errors）: ec_hte_ppci bias = 0.005, BUT ppci_alone bias = 0.004 ——  \\\"PPCI alone achieves LOWER bias than the proposed composition! EC-HTE adds nothing to bias reduction\\\"； (b) RMSE: ec_hte_ppci 0.225 vs ppci_alone 0.261 = 14% improvement， 但 reviewer 认为 \\\"this modest RMSE gain doesn't justify the additional complexity  of implementing EC-HTE on top of PPCI\\\"； (c) DGP A（covariate only）: ec_hte works well，但 reviewer 质疑： \\\"how often is covariate error the ONLY error source? In real data, outcome error always exists， making DGP C the relevant scenario — where PPCI alone suffices\\\"； (d) DSL per-subgroup 作为 baseline 未被 properly compared： \\\"if DSL per-subgroup achieves comparable results without the HB machinery,  what's the methodological contribution?\\\"； (e) \\\"Composition is necessary and sufficient\\\" claim 被 weakened to  \\\"PPCI is sufficient; EC-HTE is optional for modest RMSE gains\\\"。\\n\"\n408\t  },\n409\t  {\n410\t    \"name\": \"Multiple LLM Annotator Comparison\",\n411\t    \"description\": \"6 LLM models (GPT-3.5 through GPT-5.4) measuring misclassification heterogeneity patterns\",\n412\t    \"results\": {\n413\t      \"models_completed\": 6,\n414\t      \"all_delta_pi_above_005\": true,\n415\t      \"effective_delta_pi_range\": \"0.080 - 0.198\",\n416\t      \"worst_subgroup_consensus\": \"True_medium (5/6 models)\",\n417\t      \"spearman_significant_pairs\": 4,\n418\t      \"reviewer_verdict\": \"unsurprising — well-known that different models have different error patterns\"\n419\t    },\n420\t    \"tables\": [\n421\t      {\n422\t        \"name\": \"Table 10: Cross-Model Δπ — Reviewer Interpretation\",\n423\t        \"columns\": [\n424\t          \"Model\",\n425\t          \"Generation\",\n426\t          \"Effective Δπ\",\n427\t          \"Reviewer Comment\"\n428\t        ],\n429\t        \"rows\": [\n430\t          [\n431\t            \"GPT-3.5-turbo\",\n432\t            \"Gen 1\",\n433\t            \"0.198\",\n434\t            \"\\\"Oldest model, most error — unsurprising\\\"\"\n435\t          ],\n436\t          [\n437\t            \"GPT-4-turbo\",\n438\t            \"Gen 2\",\n439\t            \"0.149\",\n440\t            \"\\\"Better model, less error — unsurprising\\\"\"\n441\t          ],\n442\t          [\n443\t            \"GPT-4.1\",\n444\t            \"Gen 2\",\n445\t            \"0.098\",\n446\t            \"\\\"Moderate — in the regime where EC-HTE doesn't help\\\"\"\n447\t          ],\n448\t          [\n449\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n450\t            \"Gen 2\",\n451\t            \"0.080\",\n452\t            \"\\\"Low — global correction sufficient\\\"\"\n453\t          ],\n454\t          [\n455\t            \"GPT-4o-mini\",\n456\t            \"Gen 2\",\n457\t            \"0.136\",\n458\t            \"\\\"Small model, more error — expected\\\"\"\n459\t          ],\n460\t          [\n461\t            \"GPT-5.4\",\n462\t            \"Gen 3\",\n463\t            \"0.114\",\n464\t            \"\\\"Latest model still has moderate heterogeneity\\\"\"\n465\t          ]\n466\t        ]\n467\t      }\n468\t    ],\n469\t    \"figures\": [],\n470\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-008 在 worst 档下有双重解读： (1) Reviewer 可以 argue \\\"heterogeneity is diminishing with model generations  (GPT-3.5: 0.198 → GPT-5.4: 0.114), so the problem is self-solving\\\"； (2) 但在 reframed paper 中，这 IS the contribution：systematic evidence  across 6 models showing heterogeneity persists even in latest generation。 关键防御：Δπ=0.114 for GPT-5.4 仍然 above the threshold（0.10） where bias amplification is non-trivial。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 reviewer 承认 empirical finding 但否定其 significance： (a) \\\"All 6 models show Δπ > 0.05\\\" 被视为 \\\"we already know LLMs have non-uniform error patterns —  Ashwin et al. (2025) documented this, Tornberg (2024) documented this,  the entire LLM-as-annotator literature is built on this observation\\\"； (b) Δπ range 0.080-0.198 被视为 \\\"moderate, not extreme — confirming that  real-world heterogeneity falls in the regime where EC-HTE doesn't help (exp-006: K=2/moderate never crosses)\\\"； (c) \\\"Structural, not model-specific\\\" finding 被 reviewer 重新 frame： \\\"yes, heterogeneity is structural — and it's structurally MODERATE,  which is exactly the regime where global correction is sufficient\\\"； (d) 只有 4 subgroups after filtering（excluding n<10），statistical power 有限， Spearman correlations 多数 p>0.20； (e) GPT-5.4 Δπ=0.114 被 reviewer 引用为 \\\"even the best available model  has moderate heterogeneity — confirming that the MODERATE regime is the relevant one\\\"。 然而在 reframed \\\"When Debiasing Hurts\\\" 版本中，exp-008 成为 core contribution： 6 models × 3 generations 的 systematic evidence 证明 heterogeneity 是 structural phenomenon。\\n\"\n471\t  },\n472\t  {\n473\t    \"name\": \"Adaptive Expert Annotation Allocation\",\n474\t    \"description\": \"CATE-weighted allocation targeting high-CATE × high-error subgroups\",\n475\t    \"results\": {\n476\t      \"status\": \"not completed (P2 priority, cut from submission)\",\n477\t      \"reviewer_reaction\": \"missing experiment noted but not fatal\",\n478\t      \"hypothetical_if_run\": {\n479\t        \"improvement_over_uniform\": \"10-15% RMSE reduction in high-error subgroups\",\n480\t        \"aggregate_improvement\": \"5-8% overall\",\n481\t        \"still_worse_than_global_in_moderate\": true\n482\t      }\n483\t    },\n484\t    \"tables\": [\n485\t      {\n486\t        \"name\": \"Table 11: Adaptive Allocation (Hypothetical)\",\n487\t        \"columns\": [\n488\t          \"Allocation\",\n489\t          \"Aggregate RMSE\",\n490\t          \"High-Error Subgroup RMSE\",\n491\t          \"Reviewer Verdict\"\n492\t        ],\n493\t        \"rows\": [\n494\t          [\n495\t            \"Uniform\",\n496\t            \"0.12\",\n497\t            \"0.18\",\n498\t            \"\\\"Baseline\\\"\"\n499\t          ],\n500\t          [\n501\t            \"CATE-weighted\",\n502\t            \"0.11\",\n503\t            \"0.15\",\n504\t            \"\\\"Modest improvement, doesn't fix fundamental issue\\\"\"\n505\t          ],\n506\t          [\n507\t            \"Uncertainty-only\",\n508\t            \"0.115\",\n509\t            \"0.16\",\n510\t            \"\\\"Similar to CATE-weighted\\\"\"\n511\t          ]\n512\t        ]\n513\t      }\n514\t    ],\n515\t    \"figures\": [],\n516\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-009 的缺失在 worst 档下不是 major weakness，因为 reviewer 的 attack vector  是 \\\"method doesn't work on real data\\\" 而非 \\\"method could be improved with adaptive allocation\\\"。 Cutting exp-009 is correct under time constraints。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 exp-009 大概率未完成（P2 priority，5-day deadline 内无法实现）。 Reviewer 反应分两种： (a) 如果提到但未完成：\\\"the authors mention adaptive allocation as future work,  but this would be necessary to make the method practical — without it,  the budget requirements (exp-006) are prohibitive\\\"； (b) 如果完全不提：reviewer 不会注意到缺失，因为 exp-009 不是 core claim 的 evidence。 即使 exp-009 完成，worst 档 reviewer 仍会 argue： \\\"adaptive allocation improves EC-HTE but doesn't change the fundamental conclusion —  the method requires too many expert labels to be practical\\\"。 在 reframed paper 中，exp-009 可以作为 appendix-level future direction， 但不影响 core empirical contribution。\\n\"\n517\t  },\n518\t  {\n519\t    \"name\": \"Robustness to Misspecified Subgroup Structure\",\n520\t    \"description\": \"Test EC-HTE when subgroups are noisy/overlapping\",\n521\t    \"results\": {\n522\t      \"k2_coverage_hb_noise0\": 0.958,\n523\t      \"k2_coverage_hb_noise50\": 0.945,\n524\t      \"k4_coverage_hb_noise0\": 0.956,\n525\t      \"k4_coverage_hb_noise50\": 0.946,\n526\t      \"graceful_convergence\": true,\n527\t      \"hb_beats_mle_all_configs\": true,\n528\t      \"reviewer_verdict\": \"trivial result — HB shrinkage is known to be robust\"\n529\t    },\n530\t    \"tables\": [\n531\t      {\n532\t        \"name\": \"Table 12: Robustness — Coverage Across Noise Levels\",\n533\t        \"columns\": [\n534\t          \"Noise Level\",\n535\t          \"K=2 HB Coverage\",\n536\t          \"K=4 HB Coverage\",\n537\t          \"Reviewer Comment\"\n538\t        ],\n539\t        \"rows\": [\n540\t          [\n541\t            \"0%\",\n542\t            \"0.958\",\n543\t            \"0.956\",\n544\t            \"\\\"Nominal — as expected\\\"\"\n545\t          ],\n546\t          [\n547\t            \"10%\",\n548\t            \"0.948\",\n549\t            \"0.958\",\n550\t            \"\\\"Robust — as expected from HB\\\"\"\n551\t          ],\n552\t          [\n553\t            \"25%\",\n554\t            \"0.950\",\n555\t            \"0.960\",\n556\t            \"\\\"Still nominal — standard shrinkage property\\\"\"\n557\t          ],\n558\t          [\n559\t            \"50%\",\n560\t            \"0.945\",\n561\t            \"0.946\",\n562\t            \"\\\"Converges to global — by construction\\\"\"\n563\t          ]\n564\t        ]\n565\t      }\n566\t    ],\n567\t    \"figures\": [],\n568\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-010 在 worst 档下是 neutral evidence：不帮助也不伤害。 Reviewer 认为 robustness to subgroup noise 是 \\\"expected baseline behavior,  not a contribution\\\"。在 reframed paper 中可以保留在 appendix  作为 \\\"implementation validation\\\" 但不宜放在 main text。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 reviewer 对 exp-010 的评价： (a) \\\"Coverage maintained at 94.5-95.8% across all noise levels\\\" 被视为  \\\"this is the well-known property of hierarchical Bayesian shrinkage —  it automatically pools toward the global estimate when subgroup signal is noisy,  providing an automatic safeguard. This is not a finding, it's a property of the method\\\"； (b) \\\"Graceful convergence to global at 50% noise\\\" 是 \\\"by construction —  when subgroup labels are random, HB posterior concentrates on the global mean.  This is Definition 1 of partial pooling\\\"； (c) reviewer 不会 flag exp-010 as weakness，但 also 不会 credit it as contribution ——  it's \\\"expected behavior, properly verified but not interesting\\\"； (d) 在 worst 档下，exp-010 的 robustness evidence 被 counter-argued by  exp-015/016/030：\\\"robust to noise is not the same as robust to real-world conditions —  the method gracefully degrades to Global (the thing it was supposed to beat)\\\"。\\n\"\n569\t  },\n570\t  {\n571\t    \"name\": \"Causal Forest Integration\",\n572\t    \"description\": \"EC-HTE with CausalForestDML: bias reduction + debiasing-hurts amplification\",\n573\t    \"results\": {\n574\t      \"mean_abs_bias_naive\": 0.1558,\n575\t      \"mean_abs_bias_global\": 0.1073,\n576\t      \"mean_abs_bias_ec_hte\": 0.0608,\n577\t      \"mean_rmse_naive\": 0.1782,\n578\t      \"mean_rmse_global\": 0.1659,\n579\t      \"mean_rmse_ec_hte\": 0.2289,\n580\t      \"debiasing_hurts_max_ratio\": 5.9,\n581\t      \"debiasing_hurts_cases\": 9,\n582\t      \"reviewer_verdict\": \"bias-variance tradeoff unfavorable — RMSE 38% worse than global\"\n583\t    },\n584\t    \"tables\": [\n585\t      {\n586\t        \"name\": \"Table 13: CausalForest — Bias vs RMSE Tradeoff\",\n587\t        \"columns\": [\n588\t          \"Method\",\n589\t          \"Mean |Bias|\",\n590\t          \"Mean RMSE\",\n591\t          \"RMSE Rank\",\n592\t          \"Reviewer Verdict\"\n593\t        ],\n594\t        \"rows\": [\n595\t          [\n596\t            \"Naive\",\n597\t            \"0.156\",\n598\t            \"0.178\",\n599\t            \"2\",\n600\t            \"\\\"Higher bias but lower RMSE than EC-HTE\\\"\"\n601\t          ],\n602\t          [\n603\t            \"Global\",\n604\t            \"0.107\",\n605\t            \"0.166\",\n606\t            \"1 (best)\",\n607\t            \"\\\"Best RMSE, acceptable bias\\\"\"\n608\t          ],\n609\t          [\n610\t            \"EC-HTE\",\n611\t            \"0.061\",\n612\t            \"0.229\",\n613\t            \"3 (worst)\",\n614\t            \"\\\"Lowest bias but worst RMSE — unfavorable tradeoff\\\"\"\n615\t          ]\n616\t        ]\n617\t      },\n618\t      {\n619\t        \"name\": \"Table 14: Debiasing-Hurts Cases with CausalForest\",\n620\t        \"columns\": [\n621\t          \"Config\",\n622\t          \"Global/Naive Bias Ratio\",\n623\t          \"Frequency\",\n624\t          \"Reviewer Comment\"\n625\t        ],\n626\t        \"rows\": [\n627\t          [\n628\t            \"K=4/extreme/sg0\",\n629\t            \"5.9x\",\n630\t            \"1/144\",\n631\t            \"\\\"Rare extreme case\\\"\"\n632\t          ],\n633\t          [\n634\t            \"K=4/extreme/sg1-3\",\n635\t            \"1.2-2.1x\",\n636\t            \"8/144\",\n637\t            \"\\\"Moderate, manageable\\\"\"\n638\t          ],\n639\t          [\n640\t            \"All other configs\",\n641\t            \"<1.0x\",\n642\t            \"135/144\",\n643\t            \"\\\"Global correction works fine 94% of the time\\\"\"\n644\t          ]\n645\t        ]\n646\t      }\n647\t    ],\n648\t    \"figures\": [],\n649\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-011 在 worst 档下强化了 \\\"method works in theory, fails in practice\\\" narrative： 即使在 synthetic DGP 上，EC-HTE 的 RMSE 比 global 差 38%。 Reviewer 将此解读为 \\\"the fundamental tradeoff is unfavorable —  per-subgroup CM estimation noise exceeds the bias correction benefit\\\"。 在 reframed paper 中，5.9x debiasing-hurts 成为 core empirical finding： \\\"CausalForest amplifies the debiasing-hurts effect\\\" 是 novel observation， 但需要 frame 为 \\\"warning to practitioners\\\" 而非 \\\"EC-HTE solves this\\\"。\\n\\nWorst 档下 reviewer 对 exp-011 的解读高度 adversarial： (a) EC-HTE RMSE = 0.2289 vs Global RMSE = 0.1659 —— \\\"EC-HTE has 38% HIGHER RMSE  than global correction when combined with CausalForest. Lower bias comes at  unacceptable variance cost\\\"； (b) \\\"A practitioner cares about RMSE (combined bias + variance), not bias alone.  EC-HTE trades manageable bias for enormous variance, making estimates LESS useful\\\"； (c) 5.9x debiasing-hurts ratio 被 dual-interpreted： reviewer 承认 \\\"global correction can dramatically amplify bias with CausalForest\\\"  但 adds \\\"EC-HTE doesn't fix this — it has even worse RMSE, just distributed differently  (lower bias, higher variance)\\\"； (d) 9 cases of debiasing-hurts 在 144 total rows = 6.25%，被视为  \\\"rare enough that practitioners can detect and handle manually\\\"； (e) K=2/n=500 near-zero bias（0.004-0.013）被 acknowledged 但  \\\"at n=500 per subgroup, the expert budget is no longer small —  1000+ experts for 2 subgroups exceeds most research budgets\\\"。 Reviewer 会写：\\\"Table 4 reveals that EC-HTE's bias reduction comes at a steep  variance cost: mean RMSE increases 38% compared to global correction (0.229 vs 0.166).  For practitioners who care about prediction accuracy (not just unbiasedness),  this tradeoff is unfavorable. The 5.9x debiasing-hurts ratio for K=4/extreme  is concerning but occurs in only 6% of configurations.\\\"\\n\"\n650\t  }\n651\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"86283adc-5998-4c8b-8d0b-bff1cafdd1f3","uuid":"47d17ce0-3d36-45e2-a865-21848ee79c03","timestamp":"2026-05-23T20:04:52.059Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520/projects/ec_hte_llm_annotation/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260523T193110/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"HB EC-HTE Synthetic Validation\",\n    \"description\": \"Hierarchical Bayesian EC-HTE on synthetic data with full regime sweep\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mcmc_rhat_max\": 1.024,\n      \"mcmc_ess_min\": 129,\n      \"total_mc_runs\": 3600,\n      \"hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n50\": \"4-9%\",\n      \"hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n100\": \"1-2%\",\n      \"hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k4_n50_moderate\": \"6-9%\",\n      \"hb_coverage_median\": 0.93,\n      \"hb_coverage_min\": 0.87,\n      \"hyperprior_sensitivity_k4_rmse_variation\": \"~4-5%\",\n      \"reviewer_perceived_novelty\": \"none — standard James-Stein shrinkage\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: HB vs MLE RMSE Comparison (Synthetic)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Config\",\n          \"HB RMSE\",\n          \"MLE RMSE\",\n          \"Delta %\",\n          \"Reviewer Verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"K=2/extreme/n=50\",\n            \"0.091\",\n            \"0.095\",\n            \"-4.2%\",\n            \"\\\"Modest, textbook shrinkage\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K=2/extreme/n=100\",\n            \"0.079\",\n            \"0.080\",\n            \"-1.3%\",\n            \"\\\"Negligible\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K=4/extreme/n=50\",\n            \"0.99\",\n            \"1.28\",\n            \"-22.7%\",\n            \"\\\"Only works because symmetric DGP\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K=4/moderate/n=50\",\n            \"0.14\",\n            \"0.15\",\n            \"-6.7%\",\n            \"\\\"Not replicable with real CMs\\\"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 的核心 attack 不是 exp-001 结果本身不好，而是 synthetic-only validation  在 exp-004/015/016 negative 结果面前失去说服力。exp-001 被重新定性为  \\\"method works under favorable assumptions that don't hold in practice\\\"。 在 worst 档 reframe 下，exp-001 数据可以保留但重新定位为  \\\"controlled validation confirming implementation correctness\\\"，不再作为 method effectiveness 的 evidence。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下，reviewer 完全承认 HB 在 synthetic 上 works，但判定： (a) 4-9% RMSE improvement over MLE 是 \\\"modest, well-known partial pooling benefit\\\"， 任何 Bayesian textbook 都有的 James-Stein shrinkage 效应； (b) synthetic DGP 是 symmetric misclassification（FPR=FNR），人为有利于 CM inversion ——  real LLM misclassification 是 highly asymmetric（exp-004: FNR=53%），这使得 synthetic 结果不可外推； (c) coverage 0.87-0.93 in worst configs 低于 nominal 0.95，但 reviewer 不会 flag 这个 ——  他们的 attack vector 是 \\\"works on synthetic, fails on real\\\"，不是 synthetic 内部的 calibration； (d) hyperprior sensitivity 4-5% 在 K=4 被视为 \\\"acceptable but unremarkable\\\"。 总体判定：exp-001 是 competent engineering，不是 contribution。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bias Identity Verification\",\n    \"description\": \"Formal bias decomposition verification: bias = f(Δπ, Δτ) identity\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"r2_k2\": 0.9939,\n      \"r2_k4\": 0.9738,\n      \"tightness_ratio_k2_median\": 1.0027,\n      \"tightness_ratio_k4_median\": 1.0234,\n      \"debiasing_hurts_pct\": 50,\n      \"max_bias_ratio_k2\": 2.86,\n      \"max_bias_ratio_k4\": 2.41,\n      \"reviewer_novelty_assessment\": \"textbook re-derivation\",\n      \"carroll_overlap_pct\": 85\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: Bias Identity R² and Reviewer Assessment\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"K\",\n          \"R²\",\n          \"Tightness Ratio\",\n          \"Reviewer Comment\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"2\",\n            \"0.9939\",\n            \"1.0027\",\n            \"\\\"Exact — but this IS the classical result\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"4\",\n            \"0.9738\",\n            \"1.0234\",\n            \"\\\"Slight deviation from identity = finite-sample noise, not new insight\\\"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 3: Debiasing-Hurts Regions\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Scenario\",\n          \"Bias Ratio\",\n          \"Δπ threshold\",\n          \"Reviewer Comment\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"K=2/extreme\",\n            \"2.86x\",\n            \"0.1235\",\n            \"\\\"Known: overcorrection when correction model misspecified\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K=4/extreme\",\n            \"2.41x\",\n            \"0.1235\",\n            \"\\\"Same mechanism, different K\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K=2/moderate\",\n            \"1.2x\",\n            \"0.1235\",\n            \"\\\"Marginal effect — who cares?\\\"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档的 kill shot #1。当 measurement error 专家在 panel 上时， Theorem 1 的 novelty claim 被直接否定。R² = 0.99 paradoxically 证明了这 IS 一个 known result  （如果是 novel，empirical verification 不该如此 clean）。 Reframe 方向：降级为 \\\"consistent with classical ME theory, we verify the product-form  identity holds empirically across LLM annotation settings\\\"，不再 claim formal novelty。 关键：reframe 后这个 experiment 仍有价值，因为 \\\"verifying classical theory holds  in the LLM annotation context\\\" 是 valid empirical contribution，但需要 proper citation。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档的 defining assumption：reviewer panel 包含 measurement error 专家，直接指出  Theorem 1 是 Carroll et al. (2006, Ch.4) 的 special case。具体论证： (a) \\\"bias ∝ Δπ × Δτ product form\\\" 是 classical ME literature 中 \\\"bias amplification  under misspecified correction model\\\" 的 well-known result，只是 notation 不同； (b) R² = 0.99 证明 identity holds，但 \\\"verifying a known identity empirically\\\" 不是 contribution； (c) \\\"debiasing hurts in 50% of parameter space\\\" 被视为 \\\"trivially follows from the identity —  whenever Δπ and Δτ have the right sign combination, overcorrection occurs, this is Definition 4.2 in Carroll\\\"； (d) max bias ratio 2.86x / 2.41x 被视为 \\\"interesting empirically but theoretically unsurprising\\\"； (e) K=2 vs K=4 non-monotonicity（2.86 vs 2.41 for DIM）被视为 \\\"artifact of the specific estimator,  not a deep structural insight\\\"。 Reviewer 会写：\\\"The authors present Theorem 1 as a novel contribution, but the product-form  relationship between misclassification heterogeneity and bias amplification is a standard result  in the measurement error literature (Carroll et al. 2006, Fuller 1987). The empirical verification  with R²>0.97 is reassuring but not surprising.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Semi-Synthetic CSS Benchmark\",\n    \"description\": \"Semi-synthetic benchmark using TweetEval sentiment with injected CATE structure\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_subgroups\": 4,\n      \"misclass_rates\": \"S0=0.05, S1=0.10, S2=0.15, S3=0.25\",\n      \"p_z1_actual\": 0.39,\n      \"debiasing_hurts_confirmed\": true,\n      \"hb_vs_mle_n100_S3_extreme\": \"+60% RMSE improvement\",\n      \"hb_vs_mle_n50_S3_extreme\": \"-57% RMSE (HB worse)\",\n      \"boundary_condition\": \"n_expert >= 100\",\n      \"reviewer_perceived_validity\": \"low — DGP designed to favor method\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 4: Semi-Synthetic Results vs Reviewer Perception\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Config\",\n          \"HB RMSE Δ vs MLE\",\n          \"Actual Validity\",\n          \"Reviewer Perception\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"n=50/S3/extreme\",\n            \"-57%\",\n            \"Boundary condition\",\n            \"\\\"Method fails at practical budgets\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"n=100/S3/extreme\",\n            \"+60%\",\n            \"Strong result\",\n            \"\\\"Only works because P(Z=1)=0.39 and symmetric CM\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"n=250/S3\",\n            \"+5-17%\",\n            \"Moderate gain\",\n            \"\\\"Modest, not worth the complexity\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"n=500/all\",\n            \"+0.2-1.6%\",\n            \"Converged\",\n            \"\\\"At this budget, any method works\\\"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-003 的 semi-synthetic 结果在 worst 档下被 reframed 为 \\\"controlled validation  that confirms implementation correctness under favorable conditions\\\"。 关键问题不是 exp-003 结果错误，而是它不能 generalize： 当 P(Z=1) 从 0.39 降到 0.18（real data），per-subgroup expert labels  急剧减少，HB estimation noise 吞没 bias correction gain。 这 exactly 是 exp-015/016 观察到的 pattern。Reviewer 将此称为 \\\"overfitting to simulation\\\"。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 reviewer 对 exp-003 的攻击角度： (a) \\\"Semi-synthetic\\\" DGP 是 author-designed：CATE heterogeneity 是 injected 的， misclassification rates 是 hand-picked 的，treatment assignment 是 controlled 的 ——  \\\"the authors designed a DGP where their method works, then showed it works\\\"； (b) misclass_rates S0=0.05 到 S3=0.25 的 spread（Δπ=0.20）被视为 \\\"optimistic —  real-world Δπ in exp-004 is only 0.117, and in exp-012 pilot is 0.098-0.200 depending on grouping\\\"； (c) P(Z=1)=0.39 被视为 \\\"unrealistically high — CivilComments P(Z=1)=0.18,  most real datasets have severe class imbalance that exp-003 avoids\\\"； (d) n=50 boundary condition 被 acknowledged 但 n=100 recommendation 被视为  \\\"will be violated in real per-subgroup settings with K=4+ and small expert budgets\\\"； (e) 整个 semi-synthetic 在 exp-015/016 negative 面前被 recharacterized 为  \\\"overfitting to favorable simulation conditions\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Real-Data Case Study (Pattern Consistency)\",\n    \"description\": \"Real CSS dataset (UC Berkeley Hate Speech) with subgroup-varying LLM misclassification\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dataset\": \"UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech\",\n      \"n_comments\": 2496,\n      \"delta_pi\": 0.117,\n      \"global_FNR\": 0.533,\n      \"avg_abs_bias_naive\": 0.21,\n      \"avg_abs_bias_global\": 0.273,\n      \"avg_abs_bias_ec_hte\": 0.313,\n      \"ec_hte_worse_than_global\": true,\n      \"ec_hte_worse_than_naive\": true,\n      \"reviewer_verdict\": \"fatal — method fails on real data\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 5: Real-Data Results — The Fatal Evidence\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Avg |Bias|\",\n          \"Rank\",\n          \"Reviewer Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Naive\",\n            \"0.210\",\n            \"1 (best)\",\n            \"\\\"Doing nothing is better than the proposed method\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Global Corrected\",\n            \"0.273\",\n            \"2\",\n            \"\\\"Simple baseline outperforms\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EC-HTE (proposed)\",\n            \"0.313\",\n            \"3 (worst)\",\n            \"\\\"Method INCREASES bias on real data\\\"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 6: Cross-Validation with exp-015/016\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Experiment\",\n          \"Real CMs Source\",\n          \"HB vs Global RMSE\",\n          \"Verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"exp-004\",\n            \"UC Berkeley direct\",\n            \"HB worse\",\n            \"\\\"Fatal\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"exp-015\",\n            \"GPT-4.1 pilot CMs\",\n            \"HB 3-4x worse\",\n            \"\\\"Confirmed fatal\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"exp-016\",\n            \"GPT-3.5 CMs\",\n            \"HB 3.5-5x worse\",\n            \"\\\"Triply confirmed\\\"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-004 的 negative result 在 worst 档下无法 mitigate，只能 reframe。 Reframe 策略：这个 negative result BECOMES the core contribution ——  \\\"we show that standard corrections fail on real data, and we characterize exactly  why (FNR > 0.4 + P(Z=1) < 0.2 → insufficient per-subgroup positive-class expert labels)\\\"。 这是 \\\"When Debiasing Hurts\\\" 的 literal embodiment。 但 reviewer 的反驳是：\\\"problem identification without solution is not sufficient  for EMNLP main — you've shown the problem exists, now what?\\\"\\n\\n\\n这是 worst 档的 kill shot #2，也是最具破坏力的 evidence。 Reviewer 论证链： (a) EC-HTE avg |bias| = 0.313 > Global 0.273 > Naive 0.21 ——  \\\"the proposed method is WORST among all options on real data\\\"； (b) 作者 frame 为 \\\"inconclusive due to wide bootstrap CIs\\\"，但 reviewer 反驳： \\\"wide CIs are themselves evidence of the method's impracticality —  if you can't get tight enough CIs to demonstrate improvement on 2496 samples,  the method doesn't scale to realistic settings\\\"； (c) global FNR = 53% 被视为 \\\"typical of real LLM annotation\\\" 而非 \\\"edge case\\\" ——  \\\"if the method breaks whenever FNR > 0.4, it's not useful for real NLP tasks  where LLMs systematically under-detect minority categories\\\"； (d) Δπ = 0.117 is \\\"moderate, not extreme\\\" —— \\\"the method needs extreme heterogeneity  to work, but real heterogeneity is moderate\\\"； (e) exp-015 (GPT-4.1 CMs) 和 exp-016 (GPT-3.5 CMs) 用 controlled semi-synthetic  确认了 same failure pattern —— \\\"this is not a dataset artifact, it's a systematic failure\\\"。 Reviewer 会写：\\\"The real-data evaluation (Section 5.3) is the most informative result  in the paper, and it is negative. EC-HTE produces higher bias than both the naive estimator  and global correction on the UC Berkeley Hate Speech corpus. The authors attribute this  to high FNR, but high FNR is the norm in real LLM annotation tasks, not the exception.  A method that only works when the classifier is already good enough is of limited practical value.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Diagnostic Criterion Validation\",\n    \"description\": \"Diagnostic criterion: Δπ × Δτ predicts when global correction fails\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"subgroup_level_auc\": 0.833,\n      \"setting_level_auc\": 0.49,\n      \"low_pi_hurt_pct\": 84.6,\n      \"reviewer_verdict\": \"contribution failure — AUC 0.49 at actionable level\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 7: Diagnostic AUC — Claim vs Evidence\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Level\",\n          \"AUC\",\n          \"Actionable?\",\n          \"Reviewer Verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Subgroup\",\n            \"0.833\",\n            \"No (requires true CATE)\",\n            \"\\\"Circular — needs what you're trying to estimate\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Setting\",\n            \"0.490\",\n            \"Yes (but fails)\",\n            \"\\\"Worse than coin flip\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Asymmetric (exp-028)\",\n            \"0.611-0.626\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"\\\"Marginal improvement, still useless\\\"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Diagnostic 在 worst 档下被判定为 complete failure。 Reframe 策略：abandon AUC-based prediction entirely，转为  \\\"empirical rule of thumb: if Δπ > 0.10, check before applying global correction\\\"。 这不是 formal diagnostic，而是 practitioner guideline ——  类似 \\\"if VIF > 10, worry about multicollinearity\\\" 的 heuristic。 但 reviewer 可能仍会质疑：\\\"this threshold was derived from your own synthetic data,  how do we know it generalizes?\\\"\\n\\n\\nWorst 档的 kill shot #3。Reviewer 论证： (a) Setting-level AUC = 0.49 是 \\\"literally worse than random\\\" ——  \\\"the diagnostic cannot predict at the level where practitioners need to make decisions  (should I use global or stratified correction for THIS dataset?)\\\"； (b) Subgroup-level AUC = 0.833 被 dismissed： \\\"subgroup-level prediction is not actionable — a practitioner doesn't know true subgroup CATEs  at decision time, so they can't compute the diagnostic at subgroup level\\\"； (c) \\\"84.6% of low-Δπ settings hurt\\\" 是 \\\"a marginal distribution, not a prediction\\\" ——  \\\"knowing that low heterogeneity settings tend to be hurt by correction is trivially obvious  from the bias identity; the diagnostic adds no information beyond the identity itself\\\"； (d) exp-028 进一步确认 asymmetric diagnostic 也 fails（overall AUC 0.626, K=2 all zero）； (e) reviewer 会将 Claim 3 标记为 \\\"not supported by the evidence\\\" 并要求删除或  大幅 downgrade。 Reviewer 会写：\\\"The diagnostic criterion (Claim 3) is presented as a practical tool,  but its setting-level AUC of 0.49 means it cannot distinguish settings where global correction  helps from those where it hurts. The subgroup-level AUC of 0.833 is not actionable because  the required quantities (true subgroup CATEs) are unknown at decision time.  This contribution should be removed or reformulated as a negative result.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Expert Label Budget Sensitivity\",\n    \"description\": \"Systematic sweep of n_expert × K × regime for crossover point\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"crossover_K2_extreme\": 250,\n      \"crossover_K2_moderate\": \"never\",\n      \"crossover_K4_extreme\": 1000,\n      \"crossover_K4_moderate\": 2000,\n      \"hb_vs_mle_wins\": \"21/24 (87.5%)\",\n      \"reviewer_verdict\": \"impractical budgets in moderate regime\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 8: Crossover Points — Reviewer Interpretation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Config\",\n          \"Crossover n_expert\",\n          \"Practical?\",\n          \"Reviewer Comment\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"K=2/extreme\",\n            \"250\",\n            \"Marginal\",\n            \"\\\"Only practical scenario, but extreme regime is rare\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K=2/moderate\",\n            \"Never\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"\\\"Method never helps in common scenario\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K=4/extreme\",\n            \"1000\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"\\\"Budget exceeds most research projects\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K=4/moderate\",\n            \"2000\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"\\\"At 2000 labels, use experts directly\\\"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-006 在 worst 档下成为 \\\"method's own evidence against itself\\\"。 核心问题：EC-HTE 的 value proposition 是 \\\"use LLM labels cheaply + few expert labels for calibration\\\"， 但 crossover analysis 显示 calibration 本身需要大量 expert labels， 侵蚀了 cost-effectiveness argument。 Reframe：转为 \\\"budget guidelines for practitioners\\\" —— 不是 \\\"EC-HTE 需要多少 labels\\\"  而是 \\\"any correction method 在低 budget 时不如 naive\\\"。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 reviewer 的解读： (a) K=2/moderate \\\"never crosses\\\" = \\\"in the most common real-world scenario  (moderate heterogeneity, binary subgroups), EC-HTE NEVER outperforms global on RMSE\\\"； (b) K=4/extreme crossover at n=1000 experts = \\\"who has 1000 expert-labeled samples  for calibration? At that budget, just use expert labels directly for CATE estimation\\\"； (c) K=4/moderate crossover at n=2000 = \\\"absurd — 2000 expert labels for 4 subgroups  means 500/subgroup, at which point expert-only estimation is viable\\\"； (d) K=2/extreme crossover at n=250 是 \\\"the only practical scenario,  but extreme heterogeneity is rare in real data (exp-004 Δπ=0.117 is moderate)\\\"； (e) HB vs MLE 21/24 wins 被 dismissed as \\\"improvement over the wrong baseline —  the question is HB vs Global, not HB vs MLE\\\"。 总结：reviewer 将 exp-006 解读为 \\\"the method's own budget analysis shows  it's impractical except in rare extreme-heterogeneity scenarios\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"PPCI + DSL Baseline Comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"PPCI/DSL baselines, EC-HTE+PPCI composition for dual-error scenarios\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_ppci_bias\": 0.005,\n      \"dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ppci_alone_bias\": 0.004,\n      \"dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_alone_bias\": 0.178,\n      \"ec_hte_ppci_rmse\": 0.225,\n      \"ppci_alone_rmse\": 0.261,\n      \"reviewer_verdict\": \"PPCI alone achieves same bias reduction — why add EC-HTE?\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 9: DGP C (Both Errors) — PPCI vs EC-HTE+PPCI\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"|Bias|\",\n          \"RMSE\",\n          \"Reviewer Verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"PPCI alone\",\n            \"0.004\",\n            \"0.261\",\n            \"\\\"Sufficient — simpler, nearly same bias\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EC-HTE+PPCI\",\n            \"0.005\",\n            \"0.225\",\n            \"\\\"Marginal RMSE gain, not worth complexity\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EC-HTE alone\",\n            \"0.178\",\n            \"0.226\",\n            \"\\\"Cannot handle outcome error\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Naive\",\n            \"0.251\",\n            \"0.269\",\n            \"\\\"EC-HTE alone barely beats naive\\\"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-007 在 worst 档下暴露了 EC-HTE 的 marginal value： 当 PPCI 已经 available 时，EC-HTE 的 additional contribution 仅是 14% RMSE reduction。 Reviewer 将此定性为 \\\"incremental improvement over existing method,  not a new paradigm\\\"。 Reframe：在 \\\"When Debiasing Hurts\\\" 版本中，PPCI comparison  成为 \\\"what practitioners should use instead\\\" 的 recommendation。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 reviewer 的 devastating observation： (a) DGP C（both errors）: ec_hte_ppci bias = 0.005, BUT ppci_alone bias = 0.004 ——  \\\"PPCI alone achieves LOWER bias than the proposed composition! EC-HTE adds nothing to bias reduction\\\"； (b) RMSE: ec_hte_ppci 0.225 vs ppci_alone 0.261 = 14% improvement， 但 reviewer 认为 \\\"this modest RMSE gain doesn't justify the additional complexity  of implementing EC-HTE on top of PPCI\\\"； (c) DGP A（covariate only）: ec_hte works well，但 reviewer 质疑： \\\"how often is covariate error the ONLY error source? In real data, outcome error always exists， making DGP C the relevant scenario — where PPCI alone suffices\\\"； (d) DSL per-subgroup 作为 baseline 未被 properly compared： \\\"if DSL per-subgroup achieves comparable results without the HB machinery,  what's the methodological contribution?\\\"； (e) \\\"Composition is necessary and sufficient\\\" claim 被 weakened to  \\\"PPCI is sufficient; EC-HTE is optional for modest RMSE gains\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multiple LLM Annotator Comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"6 LLM models (GPT-3.5 through GPT-5.4) measuring misclassification heterogeneity patterns\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"models_completed\": 6,\n      \"all_delta_pi_above_005\": true,\n      \"effective_delta_pi_range\": \"0.080 - 0.198\",\n      \"worst_subgroup_consensus\": \"True_medium (5/6 models)\",\n      \"spearman_significant_pairs\": 4,\n      \"reviewer_verdict\": \"unsurprising — well-known that different models have different error patterns\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 10: Cross-Model Δπ — Reviewer Interpretation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Generation\",\n          \"Effective Δπ\",\n          \"Reviewer Comment\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-3.5-turbo\",\n            \"Gen 1\",\n            \"0.198\",\n            \"\\\"Oldest model, most error — unsurprising\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4-turbo\",\n            \"Gen 2\",\n            \"0.149\",\n            \"\\\"Better model, less error — unsurprising\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4.1\",\n            \"Gen 2\",\n            \"0.098\",\n            \"\\\"Moderate — in the regime where EC-HTE doesn't help\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"Gen 2\",\n            \"0.080\",\n            \"\\\"Low — global correction sufficient\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o-mini\",\n            \"Gen 2\",\n            \"0.136\",\n            \"\\\"Small model, more error — expected\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-5.4\",\n            \"Gen 3\",\n            \"0.114\",\n            \"\\\"Latest model still has moderate heterogeneity\\\"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-008 在 worst 档下有双重解读： (1) Reviewer 可以 argue \\\"heterogeneity is diminishing with model generations  (GPT-3.5: 0.198 → GPT-5.4: 0.114), so the problem is self-solving\\\"； (2) 但在 reframed paper 中，这 IS the contribution：systematic evidence  across 6 models showing heterogeneity persists even in latest generation。 关键防御：Δπ=0.114 for GPT-5.4 仍然 above the threshold（0.10） where bias amplification is non-trivial。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 reviewer 承认 empirical finding 但否定其 significance： (a) \\\"All 6 models show Δπ > 0.05\\\" 被视为 \\\"we already know LLMs have non-uniform error patterns —  Ashwin et al. (2025) documented this, Tornberg (2024) documented this,  the entire LLM-as-annotator literature is built on this observation\\\"； (b) Δπ range 0.080-0.198 被视为 \\\"moderate, not extreme — confirming that  real-world heterogeneity falls in the regime where EC-HTE doesn't help (exp-006: K=2/moderate never crosses)\\\"； (c) \\\"Structural, not model-specific\\\" finding 被 reviewer 重新 frame： \\\"yes, heterogeneity is structural — and it's structurally MODERATE,  which is exactly the regime where global correction is sufficient\\\"； (d) 只有 4 subgroups after filtering（excluding n<10），statistical power 有限， Spearman correlations 多数 p>0.20； (e) GPT-5.4 Δπ=0.114 被 reviewer 引用为 \\\"even the best available model  has moderate heterogeneity — confirming that the MODERATE regime is the relevant one\\\"。 然而在 reframed \\\"When Debiasing Hurts\\\" 版本中，exp-008 成为 core contribution： 6 models × 3 generations 的 systematic evidence 证明 heterogeneity 是 structural phenomenon。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Adaptive Expert Annotation Allocation\",\n    \"description\": \"CATE-weighted allocation targeting high-CATE × high-error subgroups\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"not completed (P2 priority, cut from submission)\",\n      \"reviewer_reaction\": \"missing experiment noted but not fatal\",\n      \"hypothetical_if_run\": {\n        \"improvement_over_uniform\": \"10-15% RMSE reduction in high-error subgroups\",\n        \"aggregate_improvement\": \"5-8% overall\",\n        \"still_worse_than_global_in_moderate\": true\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 11: Adaptive Allocation (Hypothetical)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Allocation\",\n          \"Aggregate RMSE\",\n          \"High-Error Subgroup RMSE\",\n          \"Reviewer Verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Uniform\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            \"0.18\",\n            \"\\\"Baseline\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CATE-weighted\",\n            \"0.11\",\n            \"0.15\",\n            \"\\\"Modest improvement, doesn't fix fundamental issue\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Uncertainty-only\",\n            \"0.115\",\n            \"0.16\",\n            \"\\\"Similar to CATE-weighted\\\"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-009 的缺失在 worst 档下不是 major weakness，因为 reviewer 的 attack vector  是 \\\"method doesn't work on real data\\\" 而非 \\\"method could be improved with adaptive allocation\\\"。 Cutting exp-009 is correct under time constraints。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 exp-009 大概率未完成（P2 priority，5-day deadline 内无法实现）。 Reviewer 反应分两种： (a) 如果提到但未完成：\\\"the authors mention adaptive allocation as future work,  but this would be necessary to make the method practical — without it,  the budget requirements (exp-006) are prohibitive\\\"； (b) 如果完全不提：reviewer 不会注意到缺失，因为 exp-009 不是 core claim 的 evidence。 即使 exp-009 完成，worst 档 reviewer 仍会 argue： \\\"adaptive allocation improves EC-HTE but doesn't change the fundamental conclusion —  the method requires too many expert labels to be practical\\\"。 在 reframed paper 中，exp-009 可以作为 appendix-level future direction， 但不影响 core empirical contribution。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Robustness to Misspecified Subgroup Structure\",\n    \"description\": \"Test EC-HTE when subgroups are noisy/overlapping\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"k2_coverage_hb_noise0\": 0.958,\n      \"k2_coverage_hb_noise50\": 0.945,\n      \"k4_coverage_hb_noise0\": 0.956,\n      \"k4_coverage_hb_noise50\": 0.946,\n      \"graceful_convergence\": true,\n      \"hb_beats_mle_all_configs\": true,\n      \"reviewer_verdict\": \"trivial result — HB shrinkage is known to be robust\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 12: Robustness — Coverage Across Noise Levels\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Noise Level\",\n          \"K=2 HB Coverage\",\n          \"K=4 HB Coverage\",\n          \"Reviewer Comment\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0%\",\n            \"0.958\",\n            \"0.956\",\n            \"\\\"Nominal — as expected\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"10%\",\n            \"0.948\",\n            \"0.958\",\n            \"\\\"Robust — as expected from HB\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"25%\",\n            \"0.950\",\n            \"0.960\",\n            \"\\\"Still nominal — standard shrinkage property\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"50%\",\n            \"0.945\",\n            \"0.946\",\n            \"\\\"Converges to global — by construction\\\"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-010 在 worst 档下是 neutral evidence：不帮助也不伤害。 Reviewer 认为 robustness to subgroup noise 是 \\\"expected baseline behavior,  not a contribution\\\"。在 reframed paper 中可以保留在 appendix  作为 \\\"implementation validation\\\" 但不宜放在 main text。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 reviewer 对 exp-010 的评价： (a) \\\"Coverage maintained at 94.5-95.8% across all noise levels\\\" 被视为  \\\"this is the well-known property of hierarchical Bayesian shrinkage —  it automatically pools toward the global estimate when subgroup signal is noisy,  providing an automatic safeguard. This is not a finding, it's a property of the method\\\"； (b) \\\"Graceful convergence to global at 50% noise\\\" 是 \\\"by construction —  when subgroup labels are random, HB posterior concentrates on the global mean.  This is Definition 1 of partial pooling\\\"； (c) reviewer 不会 flag exp-010 as weakness，但 also 不会 credit it as contribution ——  it's \\\"expected behavior, properly verified but not interesting\\\"； (d) 在 worst 档下，exp-010 的 robustness evidence 被 counter-argued by  exp-015/016/030：\\\"robust to noise is not the same as robust to real-world conditions —  the method gracefully degrades to Global (the thing it was supposed to beat)\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Causal Forest Integration\",\n    \"description\": \"EC-HTE with CausalForestDML: bias reduction + debiasing-hurts amplification\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mean_abs_bias_naive\": 0.1558,\n      \"mean_abs_bias_global\": 0.1073,\n      \"mean_abs_bias_ec_hte\": 0.0608,\n      \"mean_rmse_naive\": 0.1782,\n      \"mean_rmse_global\": 0.1659,\n      \"mean_rmse_ec_hte\": 0.2289,\n      \"debiasing_hurts_max_ratio\": 5.9,\n      \"debiasing_hurts_cases\": 9,\n      \"reviewer_verdict\": \"bias-variance tradeoff unfavorable — RMSE 38% worse than global\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 13: CausalForest — Bias vs RMSE Tradeoff\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Mean |Bias|\",\n          \"Mean RMSE\",\n          \"RMSE Rank\",\n          \"Reviewer Verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Naive\",\n            \"0.156\",\n            \"0.178\",\n            \"2\",\n            \"\\\"Higher bias but lower RMSE than EC-HTE\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Global\",\n            \"0.107\",\n            \"0.166\",\n            \"1 (best)\",\n            \"\\\"Best RMSE, acceptable bias\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EC-HTE\",\n            \"0.061\",\n            \"0.229\",\n            \"3 (worst)\",\n            \"\\\"Lowest bias but worst RMSE — unfavorable tradeoff\\\"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 14: Debiasing-Hurts Cases with CausalForest\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Config\",\n          \"Global/Naive Bias Ratio\",\n          \"Frequency\",\n          \"Reviewer Comment\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"K=4/extreme/sg0\",\n            \"5.9x\",\n            \"1/144\",\n            \"\\\"Rare extreme case\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K=4/extreme/sg1-3\",\n            \"1.2-2.1x\",\n            \"8/144\",\n            \"\\\"Moderate, manageable\\\"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"All other configs\",\n            \"<1.0x\",\n            \"135/144\",\n            \"\\\"Global correction works fine 94% of the time\\\"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-011 在 worst 档下强化了 \\\"method works in theory, fails in practice\\\" narrative： 即使在 synthetic DGP 上，EC-HTE 的 RMSE 比 global 差 38%。 Reviewer 将此解读为 \\\"the fundamental tradeoff is unfavorable —  per-subgroup CM estimation noise exceeds the bias correction benefit\\\"。 在 reframed paper 中，5.9x debiasing-hurts 成为 core empirical finding： \\\"CausalForest amplifies the debiasing-hurts effect\\\" 是 novel observation， 但需要 frame 为 \\\"warning to practitioners\\\" 而非 \\\"EC-HTE solves this\\\"。\\n\\nWorst 档下 reviewer 对 exp-011 的解读高度 adversarial： (a) EC-HTE RMSE = 0.2289 vs Global RMSE = 0.1659 —— \\\"EC-HTE has 38% HIGHER RMSE  than global correction when combined with CausalForest. Lower bias comes at  unacceptable variance cost\\\"； (b) \\\"A practitioner cares about RMSE (combined bias + variance), not bias alone.  EC-HTE trades manageable bias for enormous variance, making estimates LESS useful\\\"； (c) 5.9x debiasing-hurts ratio 被 dual-interpreted： reviewer 承认 \\\"global correction can dramatically amplify bias with CausalForest\\\"  但 adds \\\"EC-HTE doesn't fix this — it has even worse RMSE, just distributed differently  (lower bias, higher variance)\\\"； (d) 9 cases of debiasing-hurts 在 144 total rows = 6.25%，被视为  \\\"rare enough that practitioners can detect and handle manually\\\"； (e) K=2/n=500 near-zero bias（0.004-0.013）被 acknowledged 但  \\\"at n=500 per subgroup, the expert budget is no longer small —  1000+ experts for 2 subgroups exceeds most research budgets\\\"。 Reviewer 会写：\\\"Table 4 reveals that EC-HTE's bias reduction comes at a steep  variance cost: mean RMSE increases 38% compared to global correction (0.229 vs 0.166).  For practitioners who care about prediction accuracy (not just unbiasedness),  this tradeoff is unfavorable. The 5.9x debiasing-hurts ratio for K=4/extreme  is concerning but occurs in only 6% of configurations.\\\"\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":651,"startLine":1,"totalLines":651}}}
